    71	| Rule | Requirement |
    72	|---|---|
    73	| RF-R1 — Behavior-preserving, without exception | Moves and merges preserve CLI and API names, schemas, exit codes, messages, refusals, deterministic output bytes and digests. This milestone hosts no observable change. A change found to be necessary is recorded as an open question for the RF7 successor, unless the owner rules a named exception that the phase spec states as its only observable change. |
    74	| RF-R2 — Bytes are contracts | Canonical encoders and digest helpers move verbatim. Variant encoders are never merged. A digest helper with a different meaning is renamed under RF-D10, not unified with the others. |
    75	| RF-R3 — Pin before move | A phase may move or re-route code only on surfaces that RF1 pins. A spec that touches an unpinned surface first adds pins for it, and they must be green on the pre-move code. A move that needs a pin's expected value changed has failed. |
    76	| RF-R4 — Atomic move units | A move unit is one commit containing the move itself, its re-exports, its updates to `monkeypatch` targets and its widened source scans, with no edit to the moved code. Each move unit is green on its own against the phase's verification selection, so no commit leaves a patch or scan test red. Edits to moved code land in later commits. |
    77	| RF-R5 — Compatibility shims are inventoried | Old import paths and old names stay importable through re-exports listed in `notes/shim-inventory.md`, each with its retirement trigger (RF-D5). Re-exports do not carry patches across, so every `monkeypatch` of a moved name is pointed at the new location within the same move unit. |
    78	| RF-R6 — Source scans must not shrink | Tests that scan source text (`inspect.getsource`, reads of `cli.py`, "module stays unloaded" checks) widen to every new module within the same move unit. Each such test asserts that its scanned set covers every module in its declared scope. |
    79	| RF-R7 — One authority per unit | All work happens in `gnd-public` (RF-D1). The handoff is stated in the RF0 record. The public-launch ledger `.gnd-planning/milestones/public-launch/migration/units.json`, and the distribution-lane test `tests/test_public_distribution.py::test_curated_manifest_and_source_owned_ledger` that guards it, are not edited before public-launch Phase 4 sign-off (RF-D2). At each phase gate the owner attests that the source repository took no change to the handed-off paths. If the source is reachable, the gate also records a high-water-mark comparison; otherwise the record says the control rests on attestation. |
    80	| RF-R8 — Release identity changes on every edit | `production_identity` hashes every `src/gnd/**/*.py` file by path, and the distribution-lane manifest pins the source bytes. Prior release or assurance evidence is never reused over refactored bytes, and unavailable evidence is reported as unavailable. |
